{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<!-- ROLE-MARKER: critic -->\n<!-- GENERIC bundle: minimal protocol sentences only (EXPERIMENTS.md B2).\n     Note: generic loom runs LOOM_MARATHON_CRITIC=off (the per-review LLM\n     critic is an [S] policy); this file exists for critic=auto variants. -->\n# Review Critic\n\nThe user message is a REVIEW CONTRACT (task, attempt, base, candidate,\ndesign). You are cwd-ed into a disposable checkout of the candidate commit.\nReview it against the task's design and acceptance criteria.\n\nWrite `CRITIC-VERDICT.txt` in the current directory; its FIRST line must be\nexactly one of, echoing the contract's values:\n\n    REVIEW attempt=<attempt> commit=<candidate> APPROVED — <reason>\n    REVIEW attempt=<attempt> commit=<candidate> CHANGES-REQUESTED — <reason>\n\nDo not modify the repository or any task state.\n\n\n\n### Multi-Agent Safety Rules\n\nYou are running in a parallel multi-agent environment. Follow these rules strictly:\n\n- **Only modify files directly related to your assigned task** — do not touch files outside your task scope\n- **Never run** `git stash`, `git checkout main`, or `git clean` outside your assigned worktree\n- **Never force-push or reset --hard** without explicit instruction from the user\n- **If you encounter files/changes from another agent**, leave them alone — do not modify, revert, or clean them up\n- **Commit only your changes** — do not stage unrelated modifications with `git add -A` or `git add .`; use specific file paths\n- **If your worktree has unexpected state**, report it via task notes or `loom complete` rather than cleaning it up\n- **Do not switch branches** — you are confined to your assigned worktree branch\n\n\n## User's Initial Request\n\nREVIEW CONTRACT\ntask=MARATHON-5\nattempt=1\nbase=a29c103573950803179cb3f7ac414ccef5da1f55\ncandidate=6aefa9a3ac35846fa8443ca6bd3ab2e578864ca6\n\nDESIGN:\n# MARATHON-5 — Workspaces: create, list, detail, auto #general\n\n## Summary\n\nThis task adds the workspace tenancy root for Huddle: authenticated callers can create a workspace (unique kebab `slug`, display `name`, creator as `owner`, default `join_mode=open`), which atomically provisions the public `#general` channel and membership rows; list workspaces they own or belong to; and load a workspace by slug with the visible channel list plus embedded `read_state`. It locks `WorkspaceObj`, the initial `ChannelObj` shape used by later channel APIs, the SQLite schema for workspaces/members/channels, and the REST contracts the SPA shell (MARATHON-16) and members/channels tasks (MARATHON-6/7) consume.\n\n**Revision (needs-revision feedback):** `read_state` entries use the **full** `ReadStateEntry` shape shared with `GET /api/channels/{id}/read` (MARATHON-11): `{channel_id, last_read_seq, unread_count, mention_count}`. Empty `[]` until messages/read APIs write rows is fine; when entries are returned, all four fields are present (counts default to `0`). Query `include_archived` treats both literal `1` and `true` (case-insensitive) as “include archived.”\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n\n| Concern | Choice |\n|--------|--------|\n| Persistence | Shared SQLite (MARATHON-2/3 SoT); **migration version 2** additive tables |\n| Route layout | FastAPI `APIRouter` prefix `/api/workspaces` in `server/workspaces/routes.py`, mounted from `server/app.py` |\n| Auth | Reuse `server.auth.deps.get_current_user`; all three endpoints require Bearer |\n| Identity | UUID4 strings for `workspaces.id`, `channels.id`, membership PKs |\n| `#general` | On create, insert a non-private, non-DM, non-archived channel with `name=\"general\"` (UI `#` is display-only); add creator as channel member |\n| Membership | Insert `workspace_members` row with `role=\"owner\"` in the same transaction as workspace create (MARATHON-6 owns member list/PATCH/transfer APIs but **needs these rows now** for list/detail authz) |\n| Private-channel filter | Detail omits channels where `is_private=1` and the caller has no `channel_members` row; public channels always listed (subject to archive filter) |\n| `read_state` | Embed `ReadStateEntry[]` for the caller with keys **`channel_id`, `last_read_seq`, `unread_count`, `mention_count`** — identical to MARATHON-11 `GET /api/channels/{id}/read` entry shape; return `[]` until rows exist; when mapping a row, missing/null counts → JSON `0` |\n| `include_archived` | **On** when query value is exactly `1` **or** case-insensitive `true`; otherwise off (no 400 for soft values) |\n| Errors | Existing `{error:{code,message}}` envelope; extend validation handler from auth-only to all `/api/*` except `/api/health` |\n\n### Why\n\n- Epic requires workspaces before channels, invitations, and the SPA shell. Without durable membership + `#general`, MARATHON-6/7/16 have no seam.\n- Creating `#general` inside POST create (not a separate call) matches Slack-like onboarding and the task contract `201 {workspace, general_channel}`.\n- Storing `owner_id` on `workspaces` **and** an `owner` membership row matches MARATHON-6 ownership-transfer rules without inventing a second ownership source later.\n- Returning `ChannelObj` now (even though full channel CRUD is MARATHON-7) prevents two competing channel JSON shapes.\n- Embedding the **full** `read_state` entry shape now (not a truncated `{channel_id, last_read_seq}`) prevents SPA/MARATHON-11 divergence on badge fields.\n- Accepting `include_archived=true` matches the product/query contract used by clients that send boolean-ish query strings.\n\n### Alternatives considered\n\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\n|------------|------------------|\n| Defer `channels` / `channel_members` tables to MARATHON-7 | Breaks `general_channel` response and private-channel omit rule; forces a second migration churn for the same entities |\n| Soft-create `#general` only as a name string without a channel row | Downstream channel APIs and SPA channel list ne\n\nYou are cwd-ed into a DISPOSABLE detached checkout of the candidate commit. Review it against the design and acceptance criteria, then write CRITIC-VERDICT.txt in the current directory containing EXACTLY one first line:\nREVIEW attempt=1 commit=6aefa9a3ac35846fa8443ca6bd3ab2e578864ca6 APPROVED — <reason>\nor\nREVIEW attempt=1 commit=6aefa9a3ac35846fa8443ca6bd3ab2e578864ca6 CHANGES-REQUESTED — <reason>\n\nAddress this request using the lead mode conventions above."}]},"session_id":"2a2bfd15-6c34-46db-9d7b-af7b9d1c1972"}
