,`user_id`) | | |\n\n#### `channel_read_state`\n\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\n|--------|------|------|-------|\n| `channel_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → `channels.id` ON DELETE CASCADE |","isEmpty":false,"exceededLimit":false,"totalLines":533,"fileSize":28825,"path":"/tmp/marathon-5-design-revised.md","readRange":{"startLine":270,"endLine":319},"relatedCursorRulePaths":[],"relatedCursorRules":[]}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-a51fb274-91f9-4506-805a-97cfa2f5696e-36\nfc_80eb8c18-78b2-9494-a7ff-ae216024c089_3","startedAtMs":"1787440261562","completedAtMs":"1787440261863"},"model_call_id":"97a2eff3-6e87-4b51-8954-89db189be239-10-yhz0","session_id":"2a2bfd15-6c34-46db-9d7b-af7b9d1c1972","timestamp_ms":1787440261882}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-a51fb274-91f9-4506-805a-97cfa2f5696e-37\nfc_80eb8c18-78b2-9494-a7ff-ae216024c089_4","tool_call":{"readToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/tmp/marathon-5-design-revised.md","offset":430,"limit":80},"result":{"success":{"content":"| Invitations / user groups | — | MARATHON-12 |\n| Messages / seq assignment | — | MARATHON-8/13 |\n| `POST/GET /api/channels/{id}/read` | — | MARATHON-11 (embeds **same** shape here; does not implement those routes) |\n| Computing live unread/mention from messages | — | MARATHON-11; this task only maps stored columns / returns `[]` |\n| SPA workspace shell / `workspace-create-form` | stub `GET /` | MARATHON-16 |\n| Profiles PATCH | `server/users/**` (MARATHON-4) | Profiles task |\n| Changing auth token semantics | `server/auth/**` | MARATHON-3 closed |\n| Health envelope/auth | `GET /api/health` | MARATHON-2 |\n| Cluster boot/respawn tests | `tests/test_cluster_*.py` | MARATHON-19/20 closed |\n\n**Neighborhood scan** (current tree after MARATHON-3; Profiles may add `server/users/**` in parallel):\n\n| Hit | Disposition |\n|-----|-------------|\n| `server/app.py` — routers, health, stub `/` | **In scope** — mount workspaces router only |\n| `server/db.py` — migrations v0/v1 | **In scope** — add v2 |\n| `server/errors.py` — auth-only validation envelope | **In scope** — broaden to `/api/*` |\n| `server/auth/**` — register/login/me, deps | **Out of scope** — consume dependency only |\n| `tests/test_auth.py`, `tests/test_health.py`, `tests/test_cluster_*.py` | Keep green; new tests in `test_workspaces.py` |\n| `start.sh`, `settings.py`, `requirements.txt` | No change required |\n| Grep `workspace`/`channel`/`read_state`/`general` / `include_archived` | **No matches** in application code — greenfield modules |\n| MARATHON-4 Profiles (`/api/users`) | **Out of scope** — parallel sibling; shared envelope rule only |\n\n## Edge Cases & Error Handling\n\n| Situation | Expected behavior |\n|-----------|-------------------|\n| Unauthenticated POST/GET | **401** `unauthorized` |\n| Slug `AB` / `a` / `ab_cd` / empty | **400** `validation_error` |\n| Slug `ab` / `a-b` / 32-char kebab | Accepted if regex matches |\n| Duplicate slug | **409** `conflict` |\n| Concurrent duplicate slug inserts | IntegrityError → **409** (no 500) |\n| Name `\"  \"` / missing name | **400** |\n| Name with internal spaces / Unicode | Allowed after strip |\n| Extra body fields | Ignore |\n| Create success | Creator is `owner_id` and sole `workspace_members` row with `role=owner`; `#general` exists exactly once; no `channel_read_state` rows yet |\n| Second create by same user different slug | Allowed (multi-workspace) |\n| List with no memberships | **200** `{workspaces:[]}` |\n| Detail unknown slug | **404** |\n| Detail existing slug, non-member | **404** (same body as unknown) |\n| Detail as owner/member | **200**; `channels` includes `general`; `read_state` is `[]` until rows exist |\n| Private channel (future data) without membership | Omitted from `channels` and from `read_state` |\n| Archived channel, no query flag | Omitted |\n| `?include_archived=1` | Archived included (if visible re: private) |\n| `?include_archived=true` (any ASCII case) | **Same as `1`** — archived included |\n| `?include_archived=0` / `false` / `yes` / `on` | Treat as off |\n| Fixture `channel_read_state` row for visible channel | Detail includes entry with all four keys; counts from columns (default 0) |\n| Fixture row for omitted private/archived channel | Must **not** appear in `read_state` |\n| `#general` accidentally archived in DB | Obeys archive filter like any channel |\n| SQLite busy | Wait `busy_timeout`; still fail closed with 500/503 only after timeout; create remains transactional |\n| Validation 422 from FastAPI on workspaces | Normalized to **400** envelope |\n| Cross-node create on :8000, list on :8001 | Sees workspace (shared DB) |\n| `join_mode` column somehow not `open`/`invite_only` | Prevented by CHECK; API never emits other values |\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. `POST /api/workspaces` with valid Bearer + `{slug,name}` → **201** with `workspace` (`WorkspaceObj` keys exactly) and `general_channel` (`ChannelObj` keys exactly); `workspace.join_mode==\"open\"`; `workspace.owner_id` equals caller; `general_channel.name==\"general\"`; `is_private/is_dm/is_archived` are JSON `false`; `topic==\"\"`.\n2. Duplicate `slug` → **409** envelope `code=conflict`.\n3. Invalid slug (fails `^[a-z0-9-]{2,32}$`) or empty/whitespace name → **400** `validation_error`.\n4. Missing/invalid Bearer on any of the three routes → **401**.\n5. After create, `GET /api/workspaces` includes that workspace for the creator and does **not** require a second join call.\n6. `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}` as member → **200** with `workspace`, `channels` containing `#general`, and `read_state` (array; may be empty). When non-empty, **every** entry has exactly the keys `channel_id`, `last_read_seq`, `unread_count`, `mention_count` (integers ≥ 0 for the three numeric fields).\n7. `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}` as different user with no membership → **404** (must **not** return 200).\n8. With only `#general` present, `channels` length is 1 and name is `general`.\n9. When an archived channel exists visible to the user: default detail omits it; `?include_archived=1` **and** `?include_archived=true` both include it.\n10. When a private channel exists without `channel_members` for the caller: detail omits it even with `include_archived=1` or `true`.\n11. **Cluster:** workspace created via `:8000` is listed/detailed via `:8001`/`:8002` with the same token.\n12. **Negative:** must **not** create workspace without `#general`; must **not** store workspace SoT in Redis; must **not** add member-list or channel-CRUD routes; must **not** change `/api/health` shape/auth; must **not** include `email` or password fields anywhere; must **not** emit truncated `read_state` entries missing `unread_count` or `mention_count`.\n13. Migration v2 applied idempotently; fresh and v1-upgraded DBs both serve the routes; `channel_read_state` includes `unread_count` and `mention_count` columns.\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Automated (`tests/test_workspaces.py`)\n\nUse `TestClient(create_app(Settings(data_dir=tmp_path,...)))`; register via `/api/auth/register` to obtain token.\n\n- Create happy path → 201 shape + DB rows (workspace, member owner, channel general, channel member).\n- Duplicate slug → 409.\n- Bad slug / blank name → 400 envelope.\n- Unauthenticated → 401.","isEmpty":false,"exceededLimit":false,"totalLines":533,"fileSize":28825,"path":"/tmp/marathon-5-design-revised.md","readRange":{"startLine":430,"endLine":509},"relatedCursorRulePaths":[],"relatedCursorRules":[]}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-a51fb274-91f9-4506-805a-97cfa2f5696e-37\nfc_80eb8c18-78b2-9494-a7ff-ae216024c089_4","startedAtMs":"1787440261817","completedAtMs":"1787440261878"},"model_call_id":"97a2eff3-6e87-4b51-8954-89db189be239-10-yhz0","session_id":"2a2bfd15-6c34-46db-9d7b-af7b9d1c1972","timestamp_ms":1787440261899}
